it's great to welcome to the program  today eric garcetti who is the mayor of  los angeles california  also national co-chair for joe biden's  campaign  played an integral role i am told in the  selection of kamala harris  as the vice presidential running mate  for joe biden  to start with mayor as you've watched  the first presidential debate and the  vice presidential debate  i know that we partisans tend to see  much of what we want to see in terms of  who does who does best but  analyzing it in terms of whether it  moved the needle at all what what do you  think  you know i think it reinforced what  people think about these candidates  in the first debate i was there in  cleveland it was the first trip that i  took i had no idea  i would be exposed to uh covet 19 by our  commander-in-chief and and his  uh some of his supporters and family  that said  just if you even turned down what the  words  say watching somebody interrupt uh  the other candidate when donald trump  was interrupting joe biden it showed  that he didn't have respect not only for  him as  as his opponent but for us you know i'm  somebody who's run for office i think  it's important for you to hear what i  have to say  and what my opponent has to say because  if you have the strength of your ideas  you don't need to interrupt people and i  think  that's really the biggest contrast is  you know especially with  women who are now almost 30 points ahead  with people are just sick and tired of  the chaos  that trump has brought to this country  and he brought that same chaos to the  stage  the vice presidential debate while it  came in a slicker package  while certainly you have an accomplished  debater  in vice president pence uh he barely  answered the questions  um it was i called it flies and lies  because of the famous fly that lie  that landed on his head but all kidding  aside you know  he also interrupted this is the playbook  you know talk over people um  and deny you know the science deny when  it comes to  climate change or coped 19 deny the  facts and try to reshape them  and i think people are finally seeing  through that you can maybe convince  people before you're in power  but after four years when they can  materially see what you've done to  damage the economy  how many lives have been lost and we  feel that in a personal way i think  there's never been a clear contrast in  an election in our lifetime  yeah and and i think on the vp debate  the fact that the most memorable moment  involved in insect um  tells us you know quite a bit really i  mean it's funny but it's also a real  you know real real consideration um one  of the  sort of uh concerns that exists when  looking at  the joe by what what joe biden's first  term would look like if indeed  he gets one is that while on paper and  i've made the case that on paper joe  biden's platform  would make him the most progressive  president in history i mean on climate  he's to the left of obama  on health care he's to the left of obama  no i don't think there's any doubt there  when the news is that he's looking at a  pretty significant number of republicans  for the cabinet  you start to see some of those reluctant  maybe bernie supporters  warren supporters who do plan to vote  for biden worry  that the paper platform will not  really translate to a cabinet what is  your take on that  well first of all somebody who  co-chaired the vice presidential search  says i would believe nothing of the what  we used to call  in the navy rumor intelligence we called  it rument  there's a hundred rumors for everything  that's going on though i do believe that  those are not mutually exclusive i do  believe that uh  we will see and joe biden a president  for all of america unlike donald trump  who  looks at a state paints it a color and  decides whether he's going to help  we do need a president who will govern  for everybody regardless of whether  they're democrat  independent or republican but that  doesn't and it won't come at the expense  of the policies we've laid out in other  words we haven't put platforms out there  that we're going to run away from in an  administration you will see joe biden  and kamala harris see through  um you know getting to carbon neutral  electricity in this country by 2035  something unthinkable  to hear out of a presidential candidate  just a few years ago you will see a  massive infrastructure investment in a  new green infrastructure but i do think  it's important to have a cabinet that  reflects america  that has been a tradition generally  where you have in republican  administrations a democrat or two  and vice versa in a democratic  administration a republican or two  because  you want to have that unity in the  country but that's not going to come at  the expense of what we're going to do on  health care on housing  what we're going to do on the  environment when it comes to racial  justice those things  are part of why joe biden's running for  president and what this campaign is all  about  and what we're going to do when he wins  yeah and i guess  to the extent that nothing is given up  in order to have  a republican or two i i think that it  makes makes a lot of sense i guess the  concern  comes in when you see very ambitious  climate proposals as as you're pointing  out  if you have a republican secretary of  transportation  and energy it starts to become it starts  to at least  seem like it would be less likely but  you you think it will be  modestly calibrated and this is not  going to be uh  some some actual centrist cabinet no not  not at all i mean i  look it's good to have diverse  perspectives but when you run with a  platform your platform is your blueprint  and you don't run away from that no  matter what so you hire people who are  interested  in the boss's vision the boss is joe  biden  this isn't something done by committee  he has said if you  trust me as your next president this is  what i will  do there's no hedging of that 100 full  stop  that is what this administration will  bring to america  not because it scores political points  it's what we need our earth is burning  our fires  are record uh our air is choking we're  seeing floods everywhere  you know i chair c-40 cities which is  the 96 largest  mayors sorry cities of the world's  mayors combating climate change  so i see this every single day talking  to folks from japan and china and india  and africa  and south america and australia this is  real and finally we're going to see an  administration that steps up to this  moment not just restores  are signing on to the paris climate  accord but takes many steps forward  and engages the international  conversation that we need  it's also one last thing good not just  for the environment but good for our  economy  this is where job growth is occurring  that's what we've experienced in la  with our green new deal in los angeles  and we will see at the national level  that same  progressive and green vision um last  thing i want to touch on  from the standpoint of how this election  is going to actually happen we're seeing  record early voting although we don't  want to read too much into that because  we've seen record encouragement of early  voting  in the context of the pandemic i  wouldn't look too much at that we're  seeing  national polling that looks solid for  joe biden  but this is an electoral election not a  popular vote election so we want to be  careful there  and when you look at some key states  like pennsylvania michigan and wisconsin  two weeks out right now compared to two  weeks out four years ago  it's actually quite similar the numbers  are quite similar from what we had  between hillary clinton and donald trump  in those key states  so question one what are you looking at  in terms of your assessment and and  number two  when do you think we will have election  results the president has fear-mongered  around  it could take months i don't believe  that for a second but  it could take days it could take 10 14  days what kind of timeline are you  looking at  so those are great questions david and  you know i do think something's a little  different than four years ago i think  people are less shy about  answering in polls whether they're going  to be voting for donald trump and i do  think that this has been about as steady  polling as i've ever seen in an election  even  even in 2016 it was up and down and this  has been just  constant i think people are locked in  but we've never had an election like  this  we've never had an election in a  pandemic in the modern era  we don't know how those votes will be  counted you're right it's easy to see  the early voting but those are the most  enthusiastic people  who know how to vote who are motivated  to vote and it's really about those  folks that are busy with their lives who  are stressed by the economic situation  who might not know how to vote by mail  and have never done it those are the  folks who are really focused on and  regardless of your party i hope  everybody can protect those votes and  encourage those votes  we're using the portal iwillvote.com  where you can find out all the  information  in your state about how to vote and make  a plan to do that  and i think that if that is executed we  will win this but in terms of when we'll  know  you know there's some states that are  key swing states that are  able to start counting those votes early  in places like ohio so they're already  doing that as they receive them  other states and florida as well other  states go a little bit more slowly and  take some time in places like  pennsylvania so it all depends on what  that margin  is but i do think that look i believe  very strongly we're ahead in  every swing state we're going to win  arizona i feel with confidence if we can  execute these last couple weeks  we're going to see potentially some  pickups of new states we haven't seen in  a while  be in the democratic column and maybe  bring some back that have strayed  so we have so many different paths to  victory for joe biden  uh you know donald trump has to run the  table  and i hope that part of running the  table for him is not denying the vote  it is not uh looking at trying to  encourage  uh supporters to depress the counting of  the vote like we saw  uh in florida during the bush gore  debacle  this is a moment which all of us as  americans need to respect the vote joe  biden has said if i win or lose  i will respect the vote we still haven't  heard that out of the words of the  president  so it falls on us to save our democracy  if our president won't  yeah on on that note and i know i know  you've got to run  we know that the trump campaign has  lawyers ready to  challenge the counting of absentee  ballots and and basically go to the  courts  at midnight on november third are you  confident that the biden campaign  is also prepared sufficiently with  lawyers to challenge that  absolutely we have 17 states set up  we've been doing it for months we have  so many lawyers activists other people  who have volunteered who will do it the  right way this is not about  mob rule this is not about pressuring  folks to count or not count this is  about looking at each one carefully  making sure  every state no matter who runs the  elections adheres to the law and that  every vote is counted that's the most  basic  right that we all have as americans i  hope we can all stand up for that but  for those who would attack it  we are prepared yeah listen if joe biden  loses fairly we will deal with that um  but if it's a different scenario then  that's a very different uh america that  that we're talking about we've been  speaking with eric garcetti mayor of los  angeles california  thank you so much for your time today  thanks david really great to be with you

